# Development Workflow

Dokan Kits uses a modern development workflow with tools for code quality, testing, and building.

## PHP Development

### Composer Commands

- `composer install`: Install dependencies
- `composer phpcs`: Run PHP CodeSniffer
- `composer phpcbf`: Fix coding standards automatically
- `composer phpstan`: Run static analysis
- `composer test`: Run PHPUnit tests

### PHP Testing

- [tests/php/](mdc:tests/php): PHPUnit tests
- [phpunit.xml.dist](mdc:phpunit.xml.dist): PHPUnit configuration

## JavaScript/TypeScript Development

### NPM/Yarn Commands

- `yarn start`: Start development server
- `yarn build`: Build production assets
- `yarn lint:js`: Lint JavaScript/TypeScript
- `yarn lint:css`: Lint CSS/SCSS
- `yarn format`: Format code with Prettier

### Build Configuration

- [webpack.config.js](mdc:webpack.config.js): Webpack configuration
- [.eslintrc.js](mdc:.eslintrc.js): ESLint configuration
- [.stylelintrc.js](mdc:.stylelintrc.js): Stylelint configuration
- [tailwind.config.js](mdc:tailwind.config.js): Tailwind CSS configuration

## Git Workflow

- Feature branches: `feature/feature-name`
- Bug fixes: `fix/bug-name`
- Releases: `release/version`

## Coding Standards

- PHP: WordPress Coding Standards with some customizations
- JavaScript: WordPress JavaScript coding standards
- CSS/SCSS: WordPress CSS coding standards
